/threads/i-just-wanted-clear-skin-my-experience-with-the-blackpill.1199100/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250114120540/https://looksmax.org/threads/i-just-wanted-clear-skin-my-experience-with-the-blackpill.1199100/"},{"title":"how over is it at least clear skin jfl","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/how-over-is-it-at-least-clear-skin-jfl.1175678/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250524032312/https://looksmax.org/threads/how-over-is-it-at-least-clear-skin-jfl.1175678/"}],"news":[],"social":[{"title":"Facebook’s New Captcha Test: 'Upload a Clear Photo of Your Face'","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=15807200","site":"Hacker News","score":402,"comments":395,"year":2017}],"web":[{"title":"Clear + Brilliant — Grokipedia","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Clear_%2B_Brilliant"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Skin","chain":["Gentle fractional laser treats skin","Surface renews with little downtime","Brighter tone, finer texture"],"effect":"indirect","text":"Clear + Brilliant is a mild fractional laser people use as a starter or maintenance treatment for tone and texture, with minimal downtime. It creates tiny treated zones so the surface renews and collagen remodels. Small trials in photoaging, periorbital rejuvenation and melasma support its use."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Clear_%2B_Brilliant","lead":["Clear + Brilliant is a non-ablative fractional laser by Solta Medical, marketed as a gentle, low-downtime resurfacing option for early signs of aging, with an original 1440 nm handpiece and a 1927 nm Perméa handpiece [1]. It is often described as a \"baby Fraxel\" and is positioned as preventive skin maintenance [1].","Published human data are limited to small trials: registered studies cover photoaging, periorbital rejuvenation and melasma in groups of 14 to 40 people [2][3][4][5]. Claims of high satisfaction and millions of treatments come from manufacturer-oriented descriptions rather than from controlled trials [1]."],"infobox":[["Type","Non-ablative fractional diode laser"],["Manufacturer","Solta Medical"],["Wavelengths","1440 nm (Original), 1927 nm (Perméa) [1]"],["FDA clearance","510(k), May 2011 (per Grokipedia) [1]"],["Downtime","Described as minimal [1]"]],"sections":[{"h":"History","paras":["According to Grokipedia, Clear + Brilliant received FDA 510(k) clearance in May 2011, the Perméa handpiece was added in 2012, and the dual-wavelength Clear + Brilliant Touch launched in the US in 2021 [1]. That page is AI-generated and was not independently verified."],"subs":[]},{"h":"How it works","paras":["The device delivers fractional laser energy that creates microscopic treatment zones without removing the epidermal surface, which is said to trigger wound healing, collagen production and cell turnover [1]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Reported effects and risks","paras":["Grokipedia reports mild redness resolving within hours to a day and a typical series of four to six sessions [1]. Proponents describe improved tone, texture, radiance and pore appearance [1]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["Registered studies include a trial of combination versus laser-only treatment for photoaging (n=14) [2], a study of the 1440/1927 nm Touch device in photoaging (n=28) [3], a 1927 nm periorbital rejuvenation study (n=20) [4], and a study combining 1927 nm laser with topical cysteamine for melasma (n=20) [5]. Outcome data from these registrations are not summarised here."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"2011","event":"FDA 510(k) clearance reported [1]."},{"year":"2012","event":"Perméa 1927 nm handpiece added [1]."},{"year":"2021","event":"Clear + Brilliant Touch launched in the US [1]."}],"refs":[{"title":"Clear + Brilliant","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Clear_%2B_Brilliant","source":"Grokipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Combination Versus Laser Treatment Only (NCT03661697)","url":"https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT03661697","source":"ClinicalTrials.gov","year":2018,"type":"trial"},{"title":"Clear + Brilliant Touch 1440/1927 nm Combination Wavelength Treatment (NCT05027282)","url":"https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT05027282","source":"ClinicalTrials.gov","year":2021,"type":"trial"},{"title":"Periorbital Rejuvenation With a 1927 nm Diode Laser (NCT05811026)","url":"https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT05811026","source":"ClinicalTrials.gov","year":2023,"type":"trial"},{"title":"Topical Cysteamine and Fractional 1927nm Laser for Melasma (NCT05656833)","url":"https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT05656833","source":"ClinicalTrials.gov","year":2022,"type":"trial"}],"studies":[{"title":"Combination Versus Laser Treatment Only (NCT03661697)","url":"https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT03661697","source":"ClinicalTrials.gov","year":2018,"kind":null},{"title":"Clear + Brilliant Touch 1440/1927 nm Combination Wavelength Treatment (NCT05027282)","url":"https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT05027282","source":"ClinicalTrials.gov","year":2021,"kind":null},{"title":"Periorbital Rejuvenation With a 1927 nm Diode Laser (NCT05811026)","url":"https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT05811026","source":"ClinicalTrials.gov","year":2023,"kind":null},{"title":"Topical Cysteamine and Fractional 1927nm Laser for Melasma (NCT05656833)","url":"https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT05656833","source":"ClinicalTrials.gov","year":2022,"kind":null}],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Clear your skin without Accutane (No BS guide) BEFORE | AFTER","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/clear-your-skin-without-accutane-no-bs-guide-before-after.1750072/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251228165753/https://looksmax.org/threads/clear-your-skin-without-accutane-no-bs-guide-before-after.1750072/"},{"title":"Clear Skin Is High-Tier Aesthetic Improvement: Full Guide + Explanation","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/clear-skin-is-high-tier-aesthetic-improvement-full-guide-explanation